-- title:
--   j(q^N) lies in the localised modular ring of level Nq
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number that is prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `LiesOverPrime A q`, that is, the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid N$. Consider the ring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the residue map `IsLocalRing.residue A` from $A$ to its residue field. Let `modularRing (N * q) A` be the subring of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series `jqModC`, the $\mathfrak q$-expansion $\mathfrak q^{-1}\,(\text{numerator of } j)$, and `jqNModC (N * q)`, obtained from it by the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{Nq}$ (the ring-homomorphic `qExpand` at $Nq$). The assertion is that the series `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N`, the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{N}$ applied to `jqModC`, belongs to `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (N * q) A.toSubring (IsLocalRing.residue A)`, i.e. to `localizedAtKer` of that subring: there are $r$ and $s$ in `modularRing (N * q) A` with $s$ outside the prime ideal `redKer` attached to the coefficientwise reduction by `IsLocalRing.residue A`, such that $j(\mathfrak q^{N})\cdot s = r$.
--
--   This is the integrality statement underlying the Kronecker congruence for the modular equation $\Phi_q$ at a place of residue characteristic $q$ with $q \nmid N$: the level-$N$ $\mathfrak q$-expansion $j(\mathfrak q^{N})$, although not one of the two chosen generators at level $Nq$, becomes available after localisation at the kernel of coefficientwise reduction. It feeds [`ModularCurve.mem_modularLocalized_mul_of_not_dvd_of_exists_coeffMap_mul_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.mem_modularLocalized_mul_of_not_dvd_of_exists_coeffMap_mul_eq), where the Gauss valuation ring is compared with this localised modular ring.
